# vfs_dir: reading a folder answers its entry names, sorted. `{ROOT}` is
# template-substituted by the test runner.
#
# Coverage:
#   - an FS directory root lists its entries (0, 1)
#   - a root mount lists the union of its roots, a name the two share once (2)
#   - a walked subdirectory lists its own entries (3)
#   - a cached absence is no entry: the root reads the same after a miss
#   - a file bound into a folder is listed there, and so is a folder bound
#     into it (a mount at the name), which lists its own root
#   - a miss reads as notfound
vfs register fs {ROOT} p1
vfs register fs {ROOT} p2
vfs bindroot 1 before
vfs open 0
vfs open 1
vfs open 2
vfs walk 0 sub
vfs open 3
vfs walk 0 gone
vfs open 0
vfs register fs {ROOT} proj/extra.txt
vfs bind 3 extra.txt 5 instead
vfs bind 3 more 1 after
vfs open 3
vfs walk 3 more
vfs open 7
vfs walk 2 nowhere.txt
vfs open 9
